--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is a port of the WebUSB API to Tauri, informed by two earlier
MIT-licensed projects that solved the same underlying problem (giving a
non-Chromium desktop webview a `navigator.usb`) for different host
environments:

  - pyside6-webusb -- a QtWebEngine/PySide6 desktop-app implementation.
  - fox-webusb -- a Firefox-extension port of pyside6-webusb v0.0.4b0.

No source files were copied verbatim from either project (the runtime
architectures involved -- a Qt bridge, a Firefox WebExtension plus a native
messaging host, and a Tauri plugin -- are different enough that a line-level
port wasn't applicable), but the security model this project implements
(hardening.rs: protected interface classes, the device blocklist, filter
matching, transfer-size policy) is a direct translation of the design and,
in several specific documented cases, the exact reasoning developed across
both of those projects -- see README.md's "Relationship to prior art"
section for the specifics, including which fixes were carried forward from
which version of which project.

This project depends on, but does not redistribute:
  - Tauri (MIT/Apache-2.0) and the Tauri plugin crates it builds on.
  - nusb (MIT/Apache-2.0), for USB device access.
  - serde, serde_json, tokio, url, base64 (MIT/Apache-2.0), and
    @tauri-apps/api (MIT/Apache-2.0) on the guest-js side.

This project does not depend on or bundle Python, Qt/PySide6, pyusb, or any
Firefox-specific WebExtension API -- it is a from-scratch Rust/TypeScript
implementation against Tauri's own plugin architecture.
